      "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported a net strengthening of prior year reserves by GBP 160.3 million in 2018, representing 20.76% of its opening gross reserves. This adverse development was primarily driven by further strengthening of reserves on business written prior to 2018, particularly in short-tail lines such as North American property and Marine, which had experienced significant rate pressure in previous years. The 2016 year of account, which closed in 2018, also saw increased loss reserves across Property, Marine, and Energy divisions, impacted by a series of catastrophe events in 2017 including Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, a Mexico earthquake, and Californian wildfires, as well as smaller weather events in 2016 like hailstorms in Texas, flooding in Louisiana, and Hurricane Matthew.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "further strengthened reserves on business written prior to 2018 in short tail lines particularly North American property and Marine lines of business that had seen the most rate pressure in previous years.",
        "necessitating an increase in loss reserves across these lines of business.",
        "Competition in the marketplace continued to increase in what was already an intensely aggressive market, thus maintaining the pressure on premium rates which reduced in some classes by up to 50% over the years 2012 to 2016.",
        "decline in pricing, the cost of acquiring the business increased as the number of broker facilities in the market continued to develop and the relative amount of open market business declined.",
        "much larger catastrophic events of 2017; Hurricanes - Harvey, Irma and Maria and to a lesser extent the 2017 California wildfires.",
        "unprecedented level of small weather events which include record hailstorms in Texas, unprecedented flooding in Louisiana and Hurricane Matthew which impacted the primary insurance markets more than the reinsurance markets."
